1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,550
Fifteen thousand pages.
一万五千页。

2
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:04,930
That's one math proof, and almost nobody has read all of it.
这是一个数学证明，几乎没人把它从头读到尾。

3
00:00:04,930 --> 00:00:09,340
This week, an AI startup called Axiom says its AI agents checked every line.
这周，一家叫Axiom的AI公司说，它的AI把每一行都查了一遍，

4
00:00:09,340 --> 00:00:10,620
In twenty four days.
只用了24天。

5
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:12,670
And it found thirty four real mistakes.
还查出了34个真错误，

6
00:00:12,670 --> 00:00:14,950
One of them needed brand new math to fix.
其中一个得靠全新的数学才补得上。

7
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:15,960
Today's brain teaser:
今天的烧脑问题：

8
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:18,740
how do you check a proof too big for any human to read?
一个大到没人读得完的证明，怎么检查？

9
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:20,260
First, what was being proved?
先说它证明了什么：

10
00:00:20,260 --> 00:00:23,270
It's called the classification of finite simple groups.
有限单群分类定理。

11
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:25,750
A group is just a set of moves you can combine,
“群”就是一套能组合的动作，

12
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:28,030
like all the ways to twist a puzzle cube.
比如拧魔方的各种转法。

13
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:30,080
Simple groups are the building blocks,
单群是积木块，

14
00:00:30,080 --> 00:00:32,740
the way prime numbers build every other number.
就像质数能拼出所有的数。

15
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:35,530
The theorem says: here is the complete list of blocks.
这个定理说：积木块的完整清单就在这，

16
00:00:35,530 --> 00:00:36,630
Nothing is missing.
一块都不少。

17
00:00:36,630 --> 00:00:38,710
The list has a few infinite families,
清单里有几大无穷家族，

18
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:41,750
plus twenty six weird loners called sporadic groups.
外加26个怪家伙，叫“散在群”。

19
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:43,780
The biggest loner is called the Monster.
最大的怪家伙叫“魔群”，

20
00:00:43,780 --> 00:00:46,810
It has about eight times ten to the fifty three elements.
大约有8乘10的53次方个元素。

21
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:48,440
That's more than the number of atoms
这比整个地球的原子

22
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:49,470
in the entire Earth.
还多。

23
00:00:49,470 --> 00:00:52,150
Proving the list took about a hundred mathematicians
证完这张清单，用了大约一百位数学家，

24
00:00:52,150 --> 00:00:54,020
and more than five hundred papers.
五百多篇论文。

25
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:55,710
It started in the nineteen fifties.
五十年代开工，

26
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:58,440
People announced it was done in nineteen eighty three.
一九八三年宣布完工。

27
00:00:58,440 --> 00:00:59,840
Twist one: it wasn't done.
反转一：其实没完工，

28
00:00:59,840 --> 00:01:02,540
One gap stayed open until two thousand and four.
有个缺口一直到2004年才补上。

29
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:04,770
So how do you check fifteen thousand pages?
那一万五千页怎么查？

30
00:01:04,770 --> 00:01:07,370
Stop trusting. Start checking every single step.
别信，一步一步查。

31
00:01:07,370 --> 00:01:10,090
Axiom rewrote the proof in a language called Lean.
Axiom把证明翻译成一种叫Lean的语言，

32
00:01:10,090 --> 00:01:11,850
Lean is a super picky referee.
Lean是个超级较真的裁判。

33
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:14,560
Every step has to follow from the steps before it,
每一步都必须从前面推出来，

34
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:16,030
or Lean flat out says no.
不然Lean直接说不行。

35
00:01:16,030 --> 00:01:17,120
It's like dominoes:
就像多米诺骨牌：

36
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:19,970
if one domino is missing, the whole chain stops.
少一块，整条链就停了。

37
00:01:19,970 --> 00:01:21,190
Here's the clever part:
妙就妙在：

38
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:22,960
the AI writes, and Lean checks.
AI负责写，Lean负责查。

39
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,150
AI can make things up.
AI会瞎编，

40
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:25,950
But Lean can't be sweet talked.
可Lean不吃这一套。

41
00:01:25,950 --> 00:01:29,320
Swarms of AI agents wrote about forty three million lines.
一群AI写了大约四千三百万行，

42
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:30,600
In twenty four days.
只用了24天。

43
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,240
Twist two, the surprising one:
反转二，最意外：

44
00:01:32,240 --> 00:01:34,980
the proof people trusted for decades had cracks.
大家信了几十年的证明，有裂缝。

45
00:01:34,980 --> 00:01:37,150
Thirty four errors needed real repair.
34个错误需要真修，

46
00:01:37,150 --> 00:01:40,690
Most were typos, mislabeled tables, and missing assumptions.
大多是笔误、表格标错、漏了条件。

47
00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:43,870
But one, deep inside a piece called the Unbalanced Group Theorem,
但有一个，藏在“非平衡群定理”里，

48
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:45,850
could not be fixed with a quick patch.
改个笔误救不回来。

49
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:50,000
Axiom called in two of the original authors, Richard Lyons and Ronald Solomon,
Axiom请来当年的两位作者，莱昂斯和所罗门，

50
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,780
and they found a way around it.
绕过了这个坑。

51
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,820
That fix is now a new result of its own.
这个补丁成了一个新结果，

52
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,250
And the list of building blocks still stands.
积木清单依然成立。

53
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:56,960
Twist three:
反转三：

54
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:59,400
this might be how we check robots, too.
将来查机器人，可能也靠这个。

55
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:03,510
A self driving car or a surgical robot runs millions of lines of code.
自动驾驶、手术机器人跑着几百万行代码，

56
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:05,570
Testing can never try every case.
测试不可能试遍所有情况。

57
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:08,870
In principle, a checker like Lean can prove a rule always holds,
原理上，像Lean这样的检查器能证明一条规矩永远成立，

58
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:11,150
like this arm never swings into that wall.
比如机械臂永远不撞墙。

59
00:02:11,150 --> 00:02:13,300
Fine print: this is Axiom's own announcement.
友情提示：这是Axiom自己宣布的，

60
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:15,430
Mathematicians are still going through it.
数学家们还在细看。

61
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:17,380
And Lean only checks the question you wrote.
而且Lean只查你问的问题，

62
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:19,980
Write the question wrong, and you prove the wrong thing.
问题写错了，证出来的也是错的东西。

63
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:22,140
So how do you check a proof nobody can read?
所以，没人读得完的证明怎么查？

64
00:02:22,140 --> 00:02:24,820
Cut every step small enough for a computer to check.
把每一步切到小得电脑能查。

65
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:26,150
Fifteen thousand pages,
一万五千页，

66
00:02:26,150 --> 00:02:28,940
turned into forty three million tiny dominoes.
变成四千三百万块小骨牌。

67
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:31,070
The tallest stack of paper in math history
数学史上最高的那摞纸，

68
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:32,610
finally got a second reader.
终于有了第二个读者。

69
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:33,050
It just
只不过，

70
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:34,350
wasn't a human.
不是人。

